{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-faa08581-542e-4d5a-b864-ed73d038e9e0","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-aff78787ebf60ef4","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-4kgtstod/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8010-E001.md","content":"# Standardize manager binary reconciliation error logs with structured resource context\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic converts message-embedded resource identity to structured key-value pairs and adds the `resourceKind` field across all reconciliation error logs in the rhods-operator manager binary, and migrates the DSCInitialization (DSCI) controller from non-standard structured key names to the standard camelCase convention. It covers all five manager-binary controller tiers — the DataScienceCluster (DSC) controller, 8 component controllers (DataSciencePipelines, Kueue, ModelRegistry, Ray, SparkOperator, Trainer, TrainingOperator, TrustyAI), the module controller with its 8 module handlers (Dashboard, AIGateway, KServe, OGX, Workbenches, MLflowOperator, FeastOperator, MCPLifecycleOperator), the DSCI controller, and 5 service controllers (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup) — plus the 15 action files across 4 tiers (8 component, 3 service, 1 DSC, 3 module). It also authors and verifies the CI lint / static-analysis check covering the manager binary's converted call sites.\n\n## Scope\n\n- **Audit**: inventory all `log.Error()` call sites in reconciliation error paths across the manager binary (controllers and action files), confirming the share of calls that embed resource identity in message strings; track conversion coverage against the inventory as a checklist.\n- **Convert message-embedded identity**: for each call site embedding resource name or namespace in the message string (e.g., `log.Error(err, \"failed to reconcile Dashboard 'example' in namespace 'redhat-ods-applications'\")`), extract the identity into structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`) and remove the redundant identity from the message text.\n- **Migrate DSCI key names**: replace the non-standard structured field names `Request.Name` and `DSCInitialization` with the camelCase convention (`name`, `namespace`) in the DSCI controller's error logs.\n- **Add `resourceKind`**: add `resourceKind` as a structured field to reconciliation error logs in all manager-binary controller tiers — service controllers, module controller (all 8 module handlers), DSCI, DSC controller, and the 8 component controllers — and to all action-file error logs (`components/<name>/<name>_controller_actions.go`, `services/{auth,gateway,monitoring}/*_controller_actions.go`, `datasciencecluster/datasciencecluster_controller_actions.go`, `modules/modules_controller_actions*.go`).\n- **Cluster-scoped resources**: for cluster-scoped kinds such as DataScienceCluster and DSCInitialization, emit `name` and `resourceKind` and either omit `namespace` or set it to the empty string, so no spurious namespace value is logged.\n- **Lint enforcement for this binary's surfaces**: author and verify the CI lint rule / static-analysis check covering the manager binary's converted call sites — it flags any `log.Error` call that embeds name/namespace in message text or is missing the required structured fields.\n- **Tests**: unit tests parsing test logger output to assert field presence and correct values across the controllers and all 15 action files; a codebase grep confirming no references to the old DSCI field names remain.\n- **Backwards-compatibility verification**: before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error, confirming structured fields appear and the production log consumer stack (e.g., Loki) ingests both formats without configuration changes; identify, together with SRE/Support, any text-based alert rules that rely on changed message-string patterns and propose updates.\n- **Release notes**: document the DSCI key-name migration in release notes with before/after query examples, delivered in a single release to avoid long-term inconsistency.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Every manager-binary reconciliation error log that previously embedded resource name or namespace in the message string uses structured key-value pairs instead — measured by the CI lint rule / static analysis flagging any remaining `log.Error` calls with name/namespace embedded in message text.\n- All DSCI controller reconciliation error logs use the camelCase convention (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`) — measured by a unit test asserting the standard field names and a codebase grep confirming no `Request.Name` / `DSCInitialization` field references remain.\n- Every service controller (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup) reconciliation error log includes `resourceKind` as a structured field — measured by a unit test parsing test logger output and asserting `resourceKind` is present with the correct value.\n- Every action file error log across all 4 tiers (8 component, 3 service, 1 DSC, 3 module) includes `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` as structured fields — measured by unit tests asserting all three fields are present with correct values across all 15 action files.\n- Module controller error logs include `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` across all 8 module handlers — measured by unit tests on test logger output.\n- DSC and component controller reconciliation error logs include `resourceKind` (bundled P1 queryability enhancement over the same converted call sites) — measured by unit tests on test logger output.\n- Cluster-scoped resources emit `name` and `resourceKind` with `namespace` omitted or empty — measured by a unit test confirming no spurious namespace value is logged.\n- The CI lint / static-analysis check covering this binary's converted call sites runs in CI and fails on `log.Error` calls embedding identity in message text or missing required structured fields.\n- A before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error confirms structured fields appear and the log consumer ingests both formats without configuration changes, and text-based alert rules affected by changed message strings are identified with proposed updates handed to SRE/Support.\n- The DSCI key-name migration is documented in release notes with before/after query examples.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P0)** — manager-binary share: all manager reconciliation error logs embedding resource name/namespace in message strings converted to structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`).\n- **HLR-2 (P0)** — DSCI controller migrated from `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` to camelCase `name`/`namespace`.\n- **HLR-3 (P0)** — service controller (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup) error logs include `resourceKind`.\n- **HLR-4 (P0)** — action file error logs include `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind` across all 4 tiers (8 component + 3 service + 1 DSC + 3 module).\n- **HLR-6 (P0)** — module controller error logs include `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind` (8 module handlers).\n- **HLR-7 (P1, bundled)** — DSC and component controller error logs include `resourceKind`; bundled because it is the same `log.Error` call sites and controller files as the HLR-1 conversion pass — a separate epic would audit and edit the same files twice, and the addition is one mechanical extension of the same conversion.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":68522,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b44e8c92a9af6ce","agent_id":"aa0e7b6d17f6c27ab","session_id":"326616fc-8f4b-4f48-9d9b-9ede56865310","uuid":"4b1f5e35-4d3a-4521-8be1-69c580e8dbbe","timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:33:28.185Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8010"}
