{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-ee8c936f-3ebc-4342-bcbb-a5837bfe80c2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-981374eada3ca472","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-4kgtstod/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8010-E002.md","content":"# Standardize cloudmanager binary reconciliation error logs with structured resource context\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic applies the same structured-logging standardization to the rhods-operator cloudmanager binary, which handles multi-cloud infrastructure dependencies on non-OpenShift Kubernetes (AWS EKS, Azure AKS, CoreWeave). Its three reconciliation controllers (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) are built on the shared reconciler pattern and already receive `name`/`namespace` from controller-runtime's request logger; the remaining work is converting message-embedded resource identity in error paths to structured key-value pairs and adding `resourceKind`. This epic also authors and verifies the CI lint / static-analysis check covering the cloudmanager binary's converted call sites.\n\n## Scope\n\n- **Audit**: inventory all `log.Error()` call sites in reconciliation error paths across the cloudmanager binary's controllers, confirming which embed resource identity in message strings; track conversion coverage against the inventory.\n- **Convert message-embedded identity**: for each cloudmanager error-path call site embedding resource name or namespace in the message string, extract the identity into structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`) and remove the redundant identity from the message text.\n- **Add `resourceKind`**: add `resourceKind` as a structured field to the AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, and CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine controllers' reconciliation error logs (these controllers do not reconcile a single implied kind per controller name in cross-controller queries, so the field is required, not optional).\n- **Migrate non-standard keys (if present)**: if the audit finds non-standard structured key names in cloudmanager error paths, migrate them to the camelCase convention (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`).\n- **Lint enforcement for this binary's surfaces**: author and verify the CI lint rule / static-analysis check covering the cloudmanager binary's converted call sites — it flags any `log.Error` call that embeds name/namespace in message text or is missing the required structured fields.\n- **Tests**: unit tests parsing test logger output to assert `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` presence and correctness for each cloudmanager controller.\n- **Backwards-compatibility verification**: before/after log output comparison for a sample cloudmanager reconciliation error, confirming structured fields appear and the relevant log consumers (e.g., CloudWatch) ingest both formats without configuration changes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Every cloudmanager controller (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) reconciliation error log includes `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` as structured fields — measured by unit tests asserting field presence and correctness in test logger output.\n- No cloudmanager reconciliation error log embeds resource name or namespace in its message string — measured by the CI lint rule / static analysis flagging any remaining `log.Error` calls with identity embedded in message text.\n- The CI lint / static-analysis check covering this binary's converted call sites runs in CI and fails on `log.Error` calls embedding identity in message text or missing required structured fields.\n- A before/after log output comparison for a sample cloudmanager reconciliation error confirms structured fields appear and the log consumer ingests both formats without configuration changes.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P0)** — cloudmanager-binary share: all rhods-operator reconciliation error logs embedding resource name/namespace in message strings converted to structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`); the cloudmanager controllers' call sites are covered here.\n- **HLR-5 (P0)** — all cloudmanager controller (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) reconciliation error logs include `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` as structured fields.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":70204,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b44e8c92a9af6ce","agent_id":"aa0e7b6d17f6c27ab","session_id":"326616fc-8f4b-4f48-9d9b-9ede56865310","uuid":"9e8ed392-f79b-4103-aa61-50e94af5f64f","timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:33:42.213Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8010"}
