{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-779ced65-6b6c-4fbe-8520-62a319887e8f","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-beae06373158e2c5","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8010-4kgtstod/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8010-E003.md","content":"# Document and publish the structured log field convention\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic documents the rhods-operator structured log field convention as a contribution guideline for new controller development and publishes it as a specification for external operator adoption. It captures the three-problem diagnosis behind the change (message-embedded resource identity, non-standard DSCI key names, missing `resourceKind`), the required field set, the camelCase naming rationale, before/after code examples, and a DSCI key migration guide for operators. Publication targets the Cluster Observability Operator team's components (Loki Operator, Tempo Operator) on a voluntary-adoption basis per platform policy (overlay 0008: RHOAI does not install, manage, or control external operator dependencies), as confirmed in the source RFE approval comment.\n\n## Scope\n\nContent outline (authored inside the contribution guideline and published convention):\n\n- **Required fields**: `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` as structured key-value pairs on reconciliation error logs, including the cluster-scoped-resource rule (namespace omitted or empty).\n- **camelCase naming rationale**: alignment with controller-runtime's existing structured log key conventions.\n- **Three-problem diagnosis**: message-embedded identity in message strings, non-standard DSCI keys (`Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization`), and the missing `resourceKind` field — with the tier-specific reasoning (kind implied by controller name for component controllers vs. required for service/module/cloudmanager controllers).\n- **Before/after code examples**: converting message-embedded identity to structured KV pairs (e.g., `log.Error(err, \"failed to reconcile Dashboard 'example' ...\")` → `log.Error(err, \"reconciliation failed\", \"name\", ..., \"namespace\", ..., \"resourceKind\", \"Dashboard\")`).\n- **DSCI key migration guide**: before/after query examples for operators with existing Loki/CloudWatch queries filtering on the old `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` field names, noting the single-release transition.\n- **Optional-fields decision record**: whether the convention extends beyond `name`/`namespace`/`resourceKind` (e.g., reconciliation attempt count, error category) — a decision owned by PM / the Observability team; the guideline must record it as adopted (with field specifications) or explicitly deferred with rationale (log-volume trade-off).\n- **Publication for external adoption**: publish the convention and file tracking issues in the COO projects (Loki Operator, Tempo Operator); adoption remains at those teams' discretion per platform policy.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The contribution guideline specifies the required fields (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`), the camelCase naming rationale, and the three-problem diagnosis.\n- Before/after code examples for converting message-embedded identity to structured KV pairs and a DSCI key migration guide with before/after query examples are included.\n- The guideline is technically reviewed against the implemented logging changes — the documented convention matches the fields actually emitted by the converted manager and cloudmanager controllers and passes the CI lint rule in force on those binaries.\n- The decision on optional fields beyond `name`/`namespace`/`resourceKind` is recorded: either the additional fields are specified, or their deferral is documented with rationale.\n- The convention is published for external operator adoption and tracking issues are filed in the COO (Loki Operator, Tempo Operator) projects; adoption is voluntary and not gated by this epic.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-8 (P1)** — the structured log field convention is documented as a contribution guideline for new controller development and published for external operator adoption.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":71174,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8b44e8c92a9af6ce","agent_id":"aa0e7b6d17f6c27ab","session_id":"326616fc-8f4b-4f48-9d9b-9ede56865310","uuid":"c08ba45d-8c08-40d7-af3a-29c848af854c","timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:33:56.348Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8010"}
