{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-85338579921e7961","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E001\n3\ttitle: Standardize manager binary reconciliation error logs with structured resource\n4\t  context\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n6\tcomponent: OpenShift AI Productization\n7\tteam: ODH Operator team\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tdependencies: []\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 6\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Standardize manager binary reconciliation error logs with structured resource context\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tThis epic converts message-embedded resource identity to structured key-value pairs and adds the `resourceKind` field across all reconciliation error logs in the rhods-operator manager binary, and migrates the DSCInitialization (DSCI) controller from non-standard structured key names to the standard camelCase convention. It covers all five manager-binary controller tiers — the DataScienceCluster (DSC) controller, 8 component controllers (DataSciencePipelines, Kueue, ModelRegistry, Ray, SparkOperator, Trainer, TrainingOperator, TrustyAI), the module controller with its 8 module handlers (Dashboard, AIGateway, KServe, OGX, Workbenches, MLflowOperator, FeastOperator, MCPLifecycleOperator), the DSCI controller, and 5 service controllers (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup) — plus the 15 action files across 4 tiers (8 component, 3 service, 1 DSC, 3 module). It also authors and verifies the CI lint / static-analysis check covering the manager binary's converted call sites.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- **Audit**: inventory all `log.Error()` call sites in reconciliation error paths across the manager binary (controllers and action files), confirming the share of calls that embed resource identity in message strings; track conversion coverage against the inventory as a checklist.\n39\t- **Convert message-embedded identity**: for each call site embedding resource name or namespace in the message string (e.g., `log.Error(err, \"failed to reconcile Dashboard 'example' in namespace 'redhat-ods-applications'\")`), extract the identity into structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`) and remove the redundant identity from the message text.\n40\t- **Migrate DSCI key names**: replace the non-standard structured field names `Request.Name` and `DSCInitialization` with the camelCase convention (`name`, `namespace`) in the DSCI controller's error logs.\n41\t- **Add `resourceKind`**: add `resourceKind` as a structured field to reconciliation error logs in all manager-binary controller tiers — service controllers, module controller (all 8 module handlers), DSCI, DSC controller, and the 8 component controllers — and to all action-file error logs (`components/<name>/<name>_controller_actions.go`, `services/{auth,gateway,monitoring}/*_controller_actions.go`, `datasciencecluster/datasciencecluster_controller_actions.go`, `modules/modules_controller_actions*.go`).\n42\t- **Cluster-scoped resources**: for cluster-scoped kinds such as DataScienceCluster and DSCInitialization, emit `name` and `resourceKind` and either omit `namespace` or set it to the empty string, so no spurious namespace value is logged.\n43\t- **Lint enforcement for this binary's surfaces**: author and verify the CI lint rule / static-analysis check covering the manager binary's converted call sites — it flags any `log.Error` call that embeds name/namespace in message text or is missing the required structured fields.\n44\t- **Tests**: unit tests parsing test logger output to assert field presence and correct values across the controllers and all 15 action files; a codebase grep confirming no references to the old DSCI field names remain.\n45\t- **Backwards-compatibility verification**: before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error, confirming structured fields appear and the production log consumer stack (e.g., Loki) ingests both formats without configuration changes; identify, together with SRE/Support, any text-based alert rules that rely on changed message-string patterns and propose updates.\n46\t- **Release notes**: document the DSCI key-name migration in release notes with before/after query examples, delivered in a single release to avoid long-term inconsistency.\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- Every manager-binary reconciliation error log that previously embedded resource name or namespace in the message string uses structured key-value pairs instead — measured by the CI lint rule / static analysis flagging any remaining `log.Error` calls with name/namespace embedded in message text.\n51\t- All DSCI controller reconciliation error logs use the camelCase convention (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`) — measured by a unit test asserting the standard field names and a codebase grep confirming no `Request.Name` / `DSCInitialization` field references remain.\n52\t- Every service controller (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup) reconciliation error log includes `resourceKind` as a structured field — measured by a unit test parsing test logger output and asserting `resourceKind` is present with the correct value.\n53\t- Every action file error log across all 4 tiers (8 component, 3 service, 1 DSC, 3 module) includes `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` as structured fields — measured by unit tests asserting all three fields are present with correct values across all 15 action files.\n54\t- Module controller error logs include `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` across all 8 module handlers — measured by unit tests on test logger output.\n55\t- DSC and component controller reconciliation error logs include `resourceKind` (bundled P1 queryability enhancement over the same converted call sites) — measured by unit tests on test logger output.\n56\t- Cluster-scoped resources emit `name` and `resourceKind` with `namespace` omitted or empty — measured by a unit test confirming no spurious namespace value is logged.\n57\t- The CI lint / static-analysis check covering this binary's converted call sites runs in CI and fails on `log.Error` calls embedding identity in message text or missing required structured fields.\n58\t- A before/after log output comparison for a sample reconciliation error confirms structured fields appear and the log consumer ingests both formats without configuration changes, and text-based alert rules affected by changed message strings are identified with proposed updates handed to SRE/Support.\n59\t- The DSCI key-name migration is documented in release notes with before/after query examples.\n60\t\n61\t## HLR Traceability\n62\t\n63\t- **HLR-1 (P0)** — manager-binary share: all manager reconciliation error logs embedding resource name/namespace in message strings converted to structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`).\n64\t- **HLR-2 (P0)** — DSCI controller migrated from `Request.Name`/`DSCInitialization` to camelCase `name`/`namespace`.\n65\t- **HLR-3 (P0)** — service controller (Gateway, Auth, Monitoring, CertConfigMapGenerator, Setup) error logs include `resourceKind`.\n66\t- **HLR-4 (P0)** — action file error logs include `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind` across all 4 tiers (8 component + 3 service + 1 DSC + 3 module).\n67\t- **HLR-6 (P0)** — module controller error logs include `name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind` (8 module handlers).\n68\t- **HLR-7 (P1, bundled)** — DSC and component controller error logs include `resourceKind`; bundled because it is the same `log.Error` call sites and controller files as the HLR-1 conversion pass — a separate epic would audit and edit the same files twice, and the addition is one mechanical extension of the same conversion.\n69\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-846322d5d1dbdab9","agent_id":"aee8d03b2a70ae580","session_id":"326616fc-8f4b-4f48-9d9b-9ede56865310","uuid":"edc030bc-4de2-45fc-a7a3-18085e5c8c00","timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:35:39.687Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-85338579921e7961","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
