{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a861357a7bc50f06","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8010-E002\n3\ttitle: Standardize cloudmanager binary reconciliation error logs with structured resource\n4\t  context\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8010\n6\tcomponent: OpenShift AI Productization\n7\tteam: ODH Operator team\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tai_signals:\n11\t  change_specificity: 1\n12\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n13\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n14\t  existing_foundation: 1\n15\t  open_questions: 1\n16\t  external_dependency: 0\n17\t  human_process_gates: 0\n18\t  repo_access: 1\n19\t  architecture_claims: 1\n20\timplementation_type: null\n21\tdependencies: []\n22\tinvestigation_signals: null\n23\tai_implementability: High\n24\tai_implementability_score: 6\n25\tjira_key: null\n26\tbranch: null\n27\tgated_by: null\n28\tgate_failure_impact: null\n29\t---\n30\t# Standardize cloudmanager binary reconciliation error logs with structured resource context\n31\t\n32\t## Description\n33\t\n34\tThis epic applies the same structured-logging standardization to the rhods-operator cloudmanager binary, which handles multi-cloud infrastructure dependencies on non-OpenShift Kubernetes (AWS EKS, Azure AKS, CoreWeave). Its three reconciliation controllers (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) are built on the shared reconciler pattern and already receive `name`/`namespace` from controller-runtime's request logger; the remaining work is converting message-embedded resource identity in error paths to structured key-value pairs and adding `resourceKind`. This epic also authors and verifies the CI lint / static-analysis check covering the cloudmanager binary's converted call sites.\n35\t\n36\t## Scope\n37\t\n38\t- **Audit**: inventory all `log.Error()` call sites in reconciliation error paths across the cloudmanager binary's controllers, confirming which embed resource identity in message strings; track conversion coverage against the inventory.\n39\t- **Convert message-embedded identity**: for each cloudmanager error-path call site embedding resource name or namespace in the message string, extract the identity into structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`) and remove the redundant identity from the message text.\n40\t- **Add `resourceKind`**: add `resourceKind` as a structured field to the AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, and CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine controllers' reconciliation error logs (these controllers do not reconcile a single implied kind per controller name in cross-controller queries, so the field is required, not optional).\n41\t- **Migrate non-standard keys (if present)**: if the audit finds non-standard structured key names in cloudmanager error paths, migrate them to the camelCase convention (`name`, `namespace`, `resourceKind`).\n42\t- **Lint enforcement for this binary's surfaces**: author and verify the CI lint rule / static-analysis check covering the cloudmanager binary's converted call sites — it flags any `log.Error` call that embeds name/namespace in message text or is missing the required structured fields.\n43\t- **Tests**: unit tests parsing test logger output to assert `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` presence and correctness for each cloudmanager controller.\n44\t- **Backwards-compatibility verification**: before/after log output comparison for a sample cloudmanager reconciliation error, confirming structured fields appear and the relevant log consumers (e.g., CloudWatch) ingest both formats without configuration changes.\n45\t\n46\t## Acceptance Criteria\n47\t\n48\t- Every cloudmanager controller (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) reconciliation error log includes `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` as structured fields — measured by unit tests asserting field presence and correctness in test logger output.\n49\t- No cloudmanager reconciliation error log embeds resource name or namespace in its message string — measured by the CI lint rule / static analysis flagging any remaining `log.Error` calls with identity embedded in message text.\n50\t- The CI lint / static-analysis check covering this binary's converted call sites runs in CI and fails on `log.Error` calls embedding identity in message text or missing required structured fields.\n51\t- A before/after log output comparison for a sample cloudmanager reconciliation error confirms structured fields appear and the log consumer ingests both formats without configuration changes.\n52\t\n53\t## HLR Traceability\n54\t\n55\t- **HLR-1 (P0)** — cloudmanager-binary share: all rhods-operator reconciliation error logs embedding resource name/namespace in message strings converted to structured key-value pairs (`name`, `namespace`); the cloudmanager controllers' call sites are covered here.\n56\t- **HLR-5 (P0)** — all cloudmanager controller (AWSKubernetesEngine, AzureKubernetesEngine, CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine) reconciliation error logs include `name`, `namespace`, and `resourceKind` as structured fields.\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f61a197868ca609","agent_id":"a6fb2e371bd48465e","session_id":"326616fc-8f4b-4f48-9d9b-9ede56865310","uuid":"e79a369d-0803-42e8-9a27-217b299c4f1b","timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:38:50.795Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a861357a7bc50f06","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8010 decomposition"}
