{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"Exit code 1\n16:**Detailed**: rhods-operator serves as the central control plane for Red Hat OpenShift AI (RHOAI). It defines and reconciles a hierarchy of custom resources—DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization, and per-component CRDs such as DataSciencePipelines, Kueue, ModelRegistry, Ray, and KServe—that declaratively describe the desired state of the AI/ML platform. The operator deploys and manages each component's manifests via kustomize-based rendering and template actions, while a set of service controllers handle cross-cutting concerns: the Auth service controller manages RBAC group policies and watches for dependent namespaces (models-as-a-service, kuadrant-system), the Gateway service controller provisions a data-science gateway with kube-auth-proxy OIDC infrastructure and conditionally integrates with Istio (EnvoyFilter, DestinationRule) and OpenShift OAuth, and the Monitoring service controller deploys Prometheus proxies and collectors for platform-level observability. A companion cloudmanager binary handles cloud-provider Kubernetes engine resources (AWS, Azure, CoreWeave). The operator exposes 19 CRDs, serves admission webhooks on port 9443 with service-ca TLS, and reads the cluster APIServer TLS profile to align its own TLS configuration with the platform-wide security policy. [source: Dockerfiles/Dockerfile.konflux:56-59, cmd/main.go:480-494, internal/controller/services/auth/auth_controller.go:56-88, internal/controller/services/gateway/gateway_controller.go:40-109, pkg/tls/profile.go:151-162]\n48:| cloudmanager | Go executable | cmd/cloudmanager |\n65:CRD count scope: 18 core API CRDs; 19 total CRD/API rows including configuration and visibility APIs.\n67:| Group | Version | Kind | Scope | API Role | Purpose |\n82:| infrastructure.opendatahub.io | v1alpha1 | AWSKubernetesEngine | Cluster | Core API | Custom resource managed by rhods-operator |\n83:| infrastructure.opendatahub.io | v1alpha1 | AzureKubernetesEngine | Cluster | Core API | Custom resource managed by rhods-operator |\n84:| infrastructure.opendatahub.io | v1alpha1 | CoreWeaveKubernetesEngine | Cluster | Core API | Custom resource managed by rhods-operator |\n91:| Name | Kind | API Group | Version | Scope | Supported Model Formats | Container Images | Built-in Adapter | Source |\n137:| github.com/opendatahub-io/opendatahub-operator/pkg/scoperules | v0.0.0 | Yes |  | Go module dependency |\n361:| **Build flags (cloudmanager)** | CGO_ENABLED=${CGO_ENABLED} (variable), -tags strictfipsruntime | Dockerfiles/Dockerfile.konflux:59 |\n373:| **Non-FIPS crypto risks** | cloudmanager CGO_ENABLED uses build arg variable rather than explicit `1`; if built without CGO the binary would use pure-Go crypto | Dockerfiles/Dockerfile.konflux:59 |\n375:The manager binary is built with explicit FIPS-compliant settings (`CGO_ENABLED=1`, `GOEXPERIMENT=strictfipsruntime`), ensuring that Go's crypto operations delegate to OpenSSL on the host. The cloudmanager binary uses `-tags strictfipsruntime` but relies on a build argument for `CGO_ENABLED` rather than hardcoding it to `1`, which is a minor build-configuration risk if the argument is not provided. The operator reads the cluster-wide TLS security profile from the OpenShift APIServer and applies it to its own TLS configuration, ensuring alignment with platform TLS policy. [source: Dockerfiles/Dockerfile.konflux:56-59, pkg/tls/profile.go:151-162]\n(eval):1: == not found","is_error":true,"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bbfc51326771f9e7"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-977c398304dc1f9c","agent_id":"aa0d196540f27e353","session_id":"326616fc-8f4b-4f48-9d9b-9ede56865310","uuid":"2ec96d49-5a59-4764-a57b-95f4e5689982","timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:40:12.850Z","tool_use_result":"Error: Exit code 1\n16:**Detailed**: rhods-operator serves as the central control plane for Red Hat OpenShift AI (RHOAI). It defines and reconciles a hierarchy of custom re